  "dom_id": "step-q184178",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Prove that ${n}^{3}-2n+1$ is odd if $n$ is even.\n\nSince $n$ is even, it can be expressed as $n=\\,${{field-1}} for some integer $a.$\n\nNow, writing ${n}^{3}-2n+1$ in terms of $a,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{3}-2n+1 & ={{field-2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
